{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XFBXzKfWMNgjX2uxyucLXb","type":"tool_result","content":"--- Asymptotics 1-20\nimport OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.StatementScale\nimport Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Base\nimport Mathlib.Data.Nat.Sqrt\n\n/-! Numerical parameters for the disjoint counting reduction. -/\n\nnamespace OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace\n\n/-- The literal base-two exponent in the counting manuscript. -/\nnoncomputable def rho (n : ℕ) : ℝ :=\n  (n : ℝ) * (Real.logb 2 (Real.logb 2 n)) ^ 2 / Real.sqrt (Real.logb 2 n)\n\n/-- Exact ceiling logarithms, computed with natural-number arithmetic. -/\ndef sparsifyLambda (n : ℕ) : ℕ := Nat.clog 2 n\n\ndef sparsifyNu (n : ℕ) : ℕ := Nat.clog 2 (sparsifyLambda n)\n\ndef sparsifySchedule (n : ℕ) : ℕ :=\n  Nat.sqrt (sparsifyLambda n) / sparsifyNu n ^ 2\n\n--- Asymptotics 180-200\n      nlinarith [Nat.cast_nonneg (α := ℝ) a]\n    nlinarith [mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right haa\n      (pow_nonneg hlog0 4)]\n  apply (le_sparsifySchedule_iff hn a).2\n  exact_mod_cast ha.trans (sparsifyLambda_bounds hn).1\n\ntheorem rho_nonneg (n : ℕ) : 0 ≤ rho n := by\n  unfold rho\n  positivity\n\ntheorem runtimeScale_le_four_rho {n : ℕ} (hn : 20 ≤ n) :\n    SqrtLog.Statement.runtimeScale n ≤ 4 * rho n := by\n  let c : ℝ := Real.log 2\n  let l : ℝ := Real.logb 2 n\n  let v : ℝ := Real.logb 2 l\n  let y : ℝ := Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16)\n  have hc : 0 < c := Real.log_pos (by norm_num)\n  have hc1 : c ≤ 1 := by\n    simpa [c] using (Real.log_le_sub_one_of_pos (by norm_num : (0 : ℝ) < 2) |>.trans (by norm_num))\n  have hl : 4 ≤ l := four_le_logb hn\n  have hl0 : 0 < l := by linarith\n--- Statement.lean 1-20\nimport OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace.Asymptotics\nimport OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace.EncodingBounds\n\n/-! Numerical transport for the frozen endpoint signatures in `specification/main-theorem.md`.\nThe existence of the required finite counting program is not asserted in this module. -/\n\nnamespace OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace\n\ntheorem runtimeBound_le_eth {n k : ℕ} (F : SAT.CNF (Fin n))\n    (hw : SAT.WidthAtMost k F) (hn : 20 ≤ n) {C A : ℝ}\n    (hC : 0 ≤ C) (hA : 0 ≤ A) (d : ℕ) :\n    SqrtLog.Statement.runtimeBound C A d (Encoding.formulaBitLength F) n ≤\n      (C * ((8 * k + 7 : ℕ) : ℝ) ^ d) * ((n + F.card + 1 : ℕ) : ℝ) ^ (2 * d) *\n        (2 : ℝ) ^ ((4 * A) * rho n) := by\n  have hexponent : A * SqrtLog.Statement.runtimeScale n ≤ (4 * A) * rho n := by\n    calc\n      A * SqrtLog.Statement.runtimeScale n ≤ A * (4 * rho n) :=\n        mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (runtimeScale_le_four_rho hn) hA\n      _ = _ := by ring\n  unfold SqrtLog.Statement.runtimeBound\n--- Final 74-110\ntheorem exact_count_and_sat (k : ℕ) (hk : 2 ≤ k) :\n    ∃ (machine : Computation.PrimitiveMachine)\n      (countTape answerTape : Fin machine.tapeCount)\n      (C A S : ℝ) (d e : ℕ),\n      0 < C ∧ 0 < A ∧ 0 < S ∧ 0 < d ∧ 0 < e ∧\n      ∀ (n : ℕ) (F : SAT.CNF (Fin n)), SAT.WidthAtMost k F →\n        ∃ (time : ℕ) (final : LocatedCfg machine),\n          Computation.Trace (locatedStep machine) time\n            (locatedInit machine (Encoding.encodeCNF F)) final ∧\n          final.config.tapes countTape =\n            Turing.Tape.mk₁ ((countWord (SAT.count F)).map some) ∧\n          final.config.tapes answerTape =\n            Turing.Tape.mk₁ [some (decide (0 < SAT.count F))] ∧\n          final.config.state = Sum.inl (decide (0 < SAT.count F)) ∧\n          BinaryArithmetic.toNat (countWord (SAT.count F)) = SAT.count F ∧\n          (countWord (SAT.count F)).length ≤ n + 1 ∧\n          (time : ℝ) ≤ OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement.runtimeBound C A d\n            (Encoding.formulaBitLength F) n ∧\n          ∀ (prefixSteps : ℕ) (intermediate : LocatedCfg machine),\n            prefixSteps ≤ time →\n            Computation.Trace (locatedStep machine) prefixSteps\n              (locatedInit machine (Encoding.encodeCNF F)) intermediate →\n            (visitedSpace intermediate : ℝ) ≤\n              S * ((Encoding.formulaBitLength F : ℝ) + 1) ^ e := by\n  obtain ⟨labels, program, C, A, S, d, e, _hout, hC, hA, hS, hd, he, hrun⟩ :=\n    compiled_exact_count_and_sat k hk\n  refine ⟨GuardedCompiler.primitive program, (256 : Fin 1220), (1216 : Fin 1220),\n    C, A, S, d, e, hC, hA, hS, hd, he, ?_⟩\n  exact hrun\n\ntheorem exact_count_eth (k : ℕ) (hk : 2 ≤ k) :\n    ∃ (labels : ℕ) (program : BitProgram.Program 80 1220 labels)\n      (C A S : ℝ) (d e : ℕ),\n      program.outputStack = 1216 ∧\n      0 < C ∧ 0 < A ∧ 0 < S ∧ 0 < d ∧ 0 < e ∧\n      ∀ (n : ℕ) (F : SAT.CNF (Fin n)), 20 ≤ n → SAT.WidthAtMost k F →\n        ∃ (time : ℕ) (final : LocatedCfg (GuardedCompiler.primitive program)),\n--- docs/378\n# The Exponential Time Hypothesis is False\n\nThe following describes the scope of the Lean formalization related to the following accompanying paper(s):\n\n- [The Exponential Time Hypothesis is False](../../preprints/The-Exponential-Time-Hypothesis-is-False-October-25-2026/paper.pdf)\n\n## Scope\n\nFor fixed $k\\ge2$, Lean proves that a deterministic machine exactly counts satisfying assignments of a canonically encoded $k$-CNF on $n$ variables in time $(L+1)^{O_k(1)}2^{O_k(n(\\log\\log n)^2/\\sqrt{\\log n})}$, where $L$ is the encoding's bit length. At every step, the machine has visited at most $(L+1)^{O_k(1)}$ tape cells in total.\n\nFor $m$ clauses, the October 25 manuscript gives the sharper time bound $(n+m)^{O_k(1)}2^{O_k(n\\log\\log n/\\sqrt{\\log n})}$. When $m\\le Dn$ for fixed $D>0$, this improves to $(n+m)^{O_{k,D}(1)}2^{O_{k,D}(n/\\sqrt{\\log n})}$.\n\n## Comparator links\n\n| Result | Comparator statement |\n| --- | --- |\n| Exact counting and SAT on canonical inputs in subexponential time and polynomial space | [SubexponentialSAT.lean](../ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.lean) |\n--- grep 80 1220\nlean/OAI/Algorithms/SubexponentialSAT/SqrtLogSpace/Final